---
import ContentPage from '../../components/ContentPage.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'Is there one best route toward five stars?', answer: 'No single plan fits every restaurant. Focus on clear service, organized work areas, and the part of the workflow that currently needs attention.' },
  { question: 'What should I review when service becomes difficult?', answer: 'Follow the full order workflow and check supplies, kitchen organization, dining layout, and task management.' },
  { question: 'Can appearance changes replace restaurant organization?', answer: 'Appearance is one part of the restaurant. Keep the main service workflow readable before focusing on customization.' },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title="Karinderya 5-Star Guide"
  description="Plan a well-organized Karinderya restaurant by improving service workflow, work areas, order handling, and restaurant management."
  kicker="Restaurant performance guide"
  intro="Work toward a well-managed restaurant by keeping every part of service connected."
  parent={{ label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }}
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.beginnerGuideHero}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/', description: 'Learn the main restaurant service loop.' },
    { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/', description: 'Follow an order through preparation and service.' },
    { label: 'Restaurant Layout Guide', href: '/guides/restaurant-layout/', description: 'Organize dining, kitchen, and movement areas.' },
    { label: 'Upgrade Priority Guide', href: '/guides/upgrade-priority/', description: 'Choose improvements around current restaurant needs.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>The five-star goal is easier to approach when the restaurant operates as one connected system. Keep customer service, ingredients, cooking, serving, layout, and task management organized rather than focusing on a single item or shortcut.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Restaurant performance depends on how clearly players can follow the service workflow. Observe what happens from the moment a customer needs attention until food is served, then improve the area that repeatedly interrupts that process.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
  <p>Each restaurant system supports another. Ingredients connect with Recipes, cooking equipment supports preparation, Furniture defines the dining area, and Workers or co-op players help organize active tasks. Strong management keeps these parts understandable during service.</p>

  <h2 id="restaurant-planning-process">Restaurant Planning Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Follow a complete customer-service cycle.</li>
    <li>Identify the point where work becomes difficult to organize.</li>
    <li>Open the related Wiki Hub for that restaurant area.</li>
    <li>Make one focused adjustment.</li>
    <li>Observe the next service cycle before making another change.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="service-focus-areas">Service Focus Areas</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Orders:</strong> keep the requested food and current task easy to identify.</li>
    <li><strong>Kitchen:</strong> organize ingredients, equipment, and completed food clearly.</li>
    <li><strong>Dining area:</strong> keep customer spaces and serving routes readable.</li>
    <li><strong>Management:</strong> divide tasks between players and Worker support where appropriate.</li>
    <li><strong>Layout:</strong> preserve clear work areas and movement routes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Improve the workflow one restaurant area at a time.</li>
    <li>Keep commonly used interactions easy to identify.</li>
    <li>Review ingredient information before service becomes difficult to manage.</li>
    <li>Use related Guides instead of relying on a universal restaurant plan.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Focusing on one restaurant area while ignoring the complete workflow.</li>
    <li>Changing several systems before observing the result.</li>
    <li>Letting appearance choices make important work areas difficult to read.</li>
    <li>Adding more active tasks than the team can follow clearly.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />
</ContentPage>
